%% Lab 06, notebook 2: a host we did not write reaches our MCP server. The Agents SDK's Runner holds the conversation
%% with the model; its client, MCPServerStdio, starts chinook_server.py as its own process and speaks to it over stdio,
%% one JSON-RPC line per message. The server runs the three lookups on the read-only database. Our code lime, the model ink.
%% Export: npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i lab06_mcp_host_client_server.mmd -o lab06_mcp_host_client_server.png -b white -s 2
flowchart LR
    model[model<br/>OpenAI API]
    subgraph HOST["host: the Agents SDK"]
        direction TB
        sdk[Runner<br/>runs the loop] --> c2[client:<br/>MCPServerStdio]
    end
    subgraph SERVER["server: its own process"]
        direction TB
        srv[chinook_server.py<br/>MCPServer]
        t1[find_customer]
        t2[get_invoices]
        t3[get_support_rep]
        db[(chinook.db<br/>read-only)]
        srv --> t1 & t2 & t3
        t1 & t2 & t3 --> db
    end
    model <-->|tool calls| sdk
    c2 <-->|stdio: one JSON line<br/>per message| srv
    classDef model fill:#0B1220,color:#FFFFFF,stroke:#0B1220
    classDef code fill:#C9F24D,color:#0B1220,stroke:#0B1220
    class model model
    class srv,t1,t2,t3 code
